The spelling program can also correct abbreviations (try Mrs.), and recog
nizes many proper nouns, such as city names (Chicago), abbreviations (CA,
Feb.), and important business names (Monsanto, Chevron).  Reformatting and
re-hyphenation occur automatically when errors are corrected.




..page

                           AUTOMATIC HYPHENATION


Volkswriter 3's automatic hyphenation is just that -- truly automatic.  It
won't interrupt you asking you to specify or confirm where a hyphen should
go.  As long as you have this option turned on, every reformatting causes
re-hyphenation as well.

Automatic hyphenation uses a special dictionary to insert "soft hyphens" at
the correct place in words that cross the right margin.  Soft hyphens are
automatically removed if reformatting moves the word away from the right
margin.

The paragraph below was formatted using narrow margins.  Note where the soft
hyphens () are, and watch them disappear when we reformat it.

